{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall guard the matzot.</b> That they not come to leavening. From here they said: knead and roll in cold water. Rabbi Yoshiya says: do not read הַמַּצּוֹת [the matzot] but הַמִּצְווֹת [the commandments] — just as one does not let matzah leaven, so one does not let a commandment leaven; rather, if it comes to your hand, do it at once (ibid.)." "<b>And you shall guard this day.</b> From labor." "<b>For your generations, an everlasting statute.</b> Since דורות and חקת עולם were not said regarding labor but regarding the חֲגִיגָה, therefore Scripture repeated it here — so that you not say: the warning of כל מלאכה לא יעשה was said not for generations but only for that generation."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:40.458433466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}